========== [zero_shot] Response ==========
Here is the implementation of the `storeInfoInHeader` function in JavaScript:

```javascript
function storeInfoInHeader(infoType, infoContent, header) {
    // Mapping of information types to their corresponding HTTP header keys
    const typeMap = {
        'lang': 'Accept-Language',
        'encoding': 'Accept-Encoding',
        'cache': 'Cache-Control'
    };

    // Check if the provided infoType is valid
    if (!(infoType in typeMap)) {
        return header; // Return original header for invalid types
    }

    // Get the appropriate header key based on infoType
    const headerKey = typeMap[infoType];

    // Create a copy of the original header to avoid mutation
    const updatedHeader = { ...header };

    // Update the header with the new information content
    updatedHeader[headerKey] = infoContent;

    return updatedHeader;
}
```
